2026-08-16T12:42:31Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: The forecast compounds FY2024Q3 GAAP diluted EPS of $6.29 by +15.79% for two years, but 15.79% is just the single-year FY2021Q3→FY2022Q3 growth from your own history, not the recent Q3 trend; the most recent two-year Q3 CAGR from FY2022Q3 to FY2024Q3 is only about +1.1% annually ((1+65.6%)*(1−38.3%)≈1.0218 over two years), which would imply FY2026Q3 near $6.4/share, not $8.43.
2026-08-16T12:42:43Z    [ADI:Revenue] GATE critic: You anchored the forecast to “$3.9 billion, +/- $100 million” as FY2026 Q3 guidance, but that figure corresponds to ADI’s guidance for the following quarter (FY2026 Q4). Using the Q4 guidance midpoint as the Q3 forecast is a one-quarter shift of the period and misstates FY2026 Q3 revenue. This can be checked directly against ADI’s Q3 FY2026 earnings release, where the $3.9B ± $0.1B range is presented as next-quarter (Q4) guidance, not Q3.
2026-08-16T12:43:26Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic: Your anchor is likely wrong: you treat FY2025 Q2 net sales as $45,300m (“We reported net sales of $45.3 billion in the second quarter of fiscal 2025”) but provide no filing link, and the 4.9% you cite looks to be the back‑solved YoY from FY2024 Q2 to a synthetic FY2025 Q2. You then apply ~+4.86% again to that anchor to get FY2026 Q2, effectively compounding the same YoY growth twice. If FY2025 Q2 was not actually $45,300m, your FY2026 Q2 is overstated by roughly $2.2bn. This can be verified directly against Home Depot’s Q2 FY2025 10‑Q/press release for “Net sales.”
2026-08-16T12:43:29Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: Your “seasonal_trend” candidate is on the wrong scale: 11.6115 USD/share aligns with the sum of the year‑to‑date adjusted diluted EPS figures you cite ($6.85 and $4.70 from FY2022Q3 and FY2021Q3), which are nine‑months YTD values, not single‑quarter EPS. Mixing a YTD per‑share figure with a quarterly metric corrupts the blend (your mean 3.47437 is already biased), and switching to a weighted median to ignore the bad input just papers over the error. With an input on the wrong scale, the submitted 3.30 lacks a valid cross‑check and is not defensible for FY2026Q3 adjusted diluted EPS.
2026-08-16T12:43:49Z    [DE:Production & Precision Ag operating profit] GATE critic: Your seasonal_trend input (579.031 USDm) is essentially just the prior-year same-quarter figure (FY2025 Q3 Production & Precision Ag operating profit = $580m per Deere’s report), i.e., a like‑for‑like carry‑forward of last year’s quarter rather than an estimate of FY2026 Q3. That’s the wrong basis: you’re using a seasonal proxy instead of modeling the actual FY2026 Q3 change, so the 554.257 USDm result is anchored to the wrong period dynamics. This can be checked directly against Deere’s FY2025 Q3 segment disclosure showing $580m.
