2026-08-16T12:44:53Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional basic EPS] GATE critic: Wrong basis: the EPS was computed from statutory P&L lines (45.43 operating profit, 13.4 net finance, and a 35.1% statutory effective tax rate) and then divided by 1,590.2m shares to get 1.307p, but the target metric is pre-exceptional basic EPS. Unless those 45.43/13.4 figures and the 35.1% tax are already pre-exceptional, this mixes GAAP with adjusted and will not match the company’s pre-exceptional definition used for the 1.31p FY2025 comparator.
2026-08-16T12:45:25Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional operating profit] GATE critic: You overrode the only cited FY2026 anchor. The source says FY2026 pre-exceptional operating profit is expected to be “in line with market consensus expectations of £45.2m,” yet you submit 45.4306 GBPm—adding unsupported precision and shifting the figure by ~£0.23m. If you’re anchoring to consensus/guidance, the checkable value for FY2026 in GBPm is 45.2, not 45.4306.
